From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:59:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gfxstream/guest: stub the virtio-gpu backend on Apple

Apple has no DRM subsystem, so osCreateVirtGpuDevice and osCreateSyncHelper
were undefined and the driver did not link.

Add a Darwin platform directory that stubs them, the way Windows and Fuchsia
do. Backend selection then needs no Apple case of its own, and kumquat is asked
for through VIRTGPU_KUMQUAT as everywhere else.

Reviewed-by: Gurchetan Singh  <gurchetan.singh.foss@gmail.com>
---
 .../guest/platform/darwin/DarwinSync.cpp      | 30 +++++++++
 .../guest/platform/darwin/DarwinSync.h        | 25 +++++++
 .../guest/platform/darwin/DarwinVirtGpu.h     | 67 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../platform/darwin/DarwinVirtGpuBlob.cpp     | 43 ++++++++++++
 .../darwin/DarwinVirtGpuBlobMapping.cpp       | 14 ++++
 .../platform/darwin/DarwinVirtGpuDevice.cpp   | 39 +++++++++++
 .../guest/platform/darwin/meson.build         | 16 +++++
 src/gfxstream/guest/platform/meson.build      |  3 +
 8 files changed, 237 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/gfxstream/guest/platform/darwin/DarwinSync.cpp
 create mode 100644 src/gfxstream/guest/platform/darwin/DarwinSync.h
 create mode 100644 src/gfxstream/guest/platform/darwin/DarwinVirtGpu.h
 create mode 100644 src/gfxstream/guest/platform/darwin/DarwinVirtGpuBlob.cpp
